# ANT+ USB Dongle — application configuration

menu "ANT+ USB Dongle"

config ANT_DONGLE_RADIO_STUB
	bool "Stub out the ANT radio layer"
	help
	  Compile src/ant_stub.c in place of the real ANT stack (libant.a from
	  sdk-ant). Every ant_*() entry point becomes a no-op returning success,
	  so the USB half of the dongle — enumeration, WinUSB auto-binding and the
	  0xA4 serial bridge — can be brought up without a working ANT build.
	  Set CONFIG_ANT=n alongside this; stub.conf does both.

config ANT_DONGLE_BCD_DEVICE
	hex "Override bcdDevice in the USB device descriptor"
	default 0x0000
	range 0x0000 0xffff
	help
	  Zephyr derives bcdDevice from the kernel version, so it never changes
	  between rebuilds. Windows caches the result of its first MS OS descriptor
	  query under HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\usbflags\<vid><pid><bcd>
	  and never re-queries a device it has already given up on — so during
	  bring-up a fresh bcdDevice is the cheapest way to make Windows look
	  again. Leave at 0x0000 to keep Zephyr's default.

endmenu

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
